# Sample environment for What Loadout. Copy to `.env` and edit that copy.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is gitignored and is **yours** - nothing in this repo should ever rewrite it. This
# file is the committed, documented template instead, so a change to the variable names lands
# here where it can be reviewed.
#
# Nothing below needs to be set for the app to work. The models, their providers and the
# provider keys are chosen in the browser, on the Settings tab, and sent with each request;
# the browser is the store of record. These variables exist for two narrower jobs:
#
#   1. The CLI, which has no browser, needs somewhere to read them from.
#   2. A variable set here pins that setting for the process. A pin outranks anything the
#      Settings tab sends, and the page marks those fields so an edit that has no effect is
#      explained rather than mysterious. So leave a value commented out unless you mean it.

# Character sheet stem in data/characters. The CLI and the API agree on this default without
# a flag.
CHARACTER=lois

# --- the reasoning model ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The provider is a setting, not something inferred from the name, because the name cannot
# carry it: an Ollama model may be a Hugging Face repo id and so contains slashes too.
#
#   LLM_PROVIDER=openrouter | claude | ollama
#   LLM_MODEL=<whatever that provider calls it>
#
# With LLM_PROVIDER unset the name is still read the old way - a slash means OpenRouter - so
# an existing one-off command keeps working.
#
#   LLM_PROVIDER=openrouter
#   LLM_MODEL=deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017
#
#   LLM_PROVIDER=claude
#   LLM_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-5
#
#   LLM_PROVIDER=ollama
#   LLM_MODEL=hf.co/mradermacher/RollMind-v1-gemma3-12b-GGUF:Q4_K_M

# --- the fast model, for one-line questions ---------------------------------------------
# An independent setting rather than a modifier on the first. Unset means the reasoning model
# answers instead, so this is optional. The provider falls back to LLM_PROVIDER.
#
#   LLM_PROVIDER_FAST=ollama
#   LLM_MODEL_FAST=qwen2.5-coder:1.5b-base
#   LLM_MODEL_FAST=deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash-0731

# --- provider keys -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Each remote provider needs its own key, and a provider whose key is absent or unusable
# cannot run - the server falls back to Ollama and says why.
#
#   OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-...
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# --- the local fallback ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where the server lands when a chosen provider cannot run, and the model used when nothing
# else is set. Needs no key. The embeddings model is separate and always local.
#
#   OLLAMA_MODEL=qwen3.5:4b
#   OLLAMA_HOST=http://127.0.0.1:11434